     };

     ttiimmeerraadddd() and ttiimmeessppeeccaadddd() add the time information stored in _a to _b
     and store the result in _r_e_s.  The results are simplified such that the
     value of _r_e_s_-_>_t_v___u_s_e_c or _r_e_s_-_>_t_v___n_s_e_c is always less than 1 second.

     ttiimmeerrssuubb() and ttiimmeessppeeccssuubb() subtract the time information stored in _b
     from _a and store the result in _r_e_s.

     ttiimmeerrcclleeaarr() and ttiimmeessppeecccclleeaarr() initialize their argument to midnight (0
     hour) January 1st, 1970 (the Epoch).

     ttiimmeerriisssseett() and ttiimmeessppeecciisssseett() return true if their argument is set to
